---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Statutory Educational Disclaimer & Limitations"
  description="Important legal disclaimer regarding the non-commercial educational nature of ZeroDebt India. Content does not constitute formal legal counsel or debt settlement brokerage."
  showSidebars={false}
>
  <div class="page-header" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem auto; text-align: center;">
    <span class="meta-tag">Legal Terms</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">Statutory Disclaimer & Educational Notice</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      ZeroDebt India is a public informational resource operated for educational and computational analysis purposes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div class="callout-box alert">
      <div class="callout-title">Not Formal Legal or Financial Advice</div>
      <p style="margin: 0;">
        The materials, statutory analyses, letter templates, and calculators provided on ZeroDebt India do not constitute legal advice, advocate-client representation, financial underwriting, or debt settlement services. Users must consult licensed advocates or certified financial planners for individualized representation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Computational Simulations as Illustrative Models</h2>
    <p>
      Calculations generated by our Multi-Loan Avalanche / Snowball Simulator and Credit Card Interest Payoff Calculator rely on user-supplied numbers, standard compound interest formulas, and theoretical reducing-balance amortisation schedules. 
    </p>
    <p>
      Actual lender statements may vary based on exact billing cycle length (30 vs 31 days), bank-specific holiday leap-year conventions, customized late-fee slabs, or specific contractual clauses in individual loan agreements.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Non-Intermediation & No Brokerage</h2>
    <p>
      ZeroDebt India does not negotiate loans with commercial banks on behalf of borrowers, does not collect payments, and does not operate as a debt settlement or recovery agency. We charge zero fees to consumers and maintain zero corporate affiliations with any lending institution or debt collection firm.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Judicial and Regulatory Interpretation</h2>
    <p>
      While our legal articles accurately summarize current Acts of Parliament (SARFAESI Act 2002, Negotiable Instruments Act 1881, Payment and Settlement Systems Act 2007) and Reserve Bank of India Master Directions, the judicial interpretation of these statutes remains subject to the jurisdictional discretion of Magistrate Courts, Debt Recovery Tribunals (DRT), High Courts, and the Supreme Court of India.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
